WEBVTT

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:27.180
It's 2 AM, the city glows

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.700
A thousand warnings on my phone

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:31.940
Somebody says we ought to stop

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:34.680
Somebody says we're too far gone

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:37.000
And you ask me what I believe

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:39.430
While rain is running down the street

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:41.780
I don't know how the story ends

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.020
But I know who I want with me

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:46.230
If there's a switch, who's holding on?

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:48.730
If there's a door, who holds the key?

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.360
And if we're building something bigger

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:53.480
Will there be room for you and me?

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:56.350
Nobody owns tomorrow

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:58.710
Nobody owns the sky

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:00.970
We're just trying to find a reason

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.630
To keep these little lights alive

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:06.140
And if the whole world changes

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.560
Before the morning light

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:11.130
Leave a little room for everyone

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:13.270
On the other side

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:32.790
On the other side

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:44.790
Another promise on a screen

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:47.180
Another beautiful machine

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.560
Another voice that tells us why

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:52.220
We have to choose a side

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:54.850
But somewhere underneath the noise

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:57.250
A million little human voices

00:01:57.320 --> 00:01:59.110
Are singing something out of tune

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:01.560
And making something beautiful

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:04.130
If there's a switch, who's holding on?

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:06.550
If there's a door, who holds the key?

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:09.150
And if we're building something bigger

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:11.300
Will there be room for you and me?

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:14.120
Nobody owns tomorrow

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:16.440
Nobody owns the sky

00:02:16.850 --> 00:02:18.770
We're just trying to find a reason

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:21.390
To keep these little lights alive

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:23.850
And if the whole world changes

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:26.320
Before the morning light

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:28.920
Leave a little room for everyone

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:31.090
On the other side

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:40.870
On the other side

00:02:50.990 --> 00:02:52.940
Maybe we're afraid of falling

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:55.200
Maybe we're afraid to fly

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:57.970
Maybe all the answers

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:00.950
Are just questions in disguise

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:06.330
But I can hear you calling...

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:12.510
Nobody owns tomorrow!

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:14.870
Nobody owns the sky!

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:17.150
We're just trying to find a reason

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:19.790
To keep these little lights alive!

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:22.290
And if the whole world changes

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:24.720
Before the morning light

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:27.340
Leave a little room for everyone

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:29.800
On the other side!

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.990
On the other side...

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:49.810
Nobody owns tomorrow...

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:01.260
Nobody owns tomorrow...

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:06.090
Nobody owns tomorrow...
